; Clean. `blit` and `reduce` each exist in exactly one target, so each
; reference has one reading. `auto` exists in *both* pipeline targets,
; but `mode`'s union tries the `auto-mode` member set first and it wins —
; the slot denotes the sentinel, not a pipeline, so alternative order
; decided nothing about which entity is meant and nothing warns.
;
; The pair to `union-ambiguous`: same schema shape, no collision that
; reaches a reference.
